(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[28 1 "// _ssl's SSL objects (queue 209): _SSLSocket over a socket or two MemoryBIOs, SSLSession and MemoryBIO."] [29 1 "//"] [30 1 "// The pipe adapter. Go's tls.Conn wants a net.Conn it may block on; OpenSSL's callers (ssl.py over a"] [31 1 "// non-blocking socket, asyncio's SSLProtocol over MemoryBIOs) want SSL_ERROR_WANT_READ and an operation"] [32 1 "// resumed by the next call. So each SSL object runs its tls.Conn in a goroutine of its own (the engine) over"] [33 1 "// an in-memory transport: the engine's Read takes what the Python side fed it and, when there is nothing,"] [34 1 "// tells the Python side it wants input and waits; its Write appends to the bytes to send. Control alternates"] [35 1 "// strictly (the Python thread waits on the engine's event with the GIL released, the engine waits on the"] [36 1 "// Python side's resume), so the engine touches no Python object and the transport's buffers have one owner at"] [37 1 "// a time. The Python side feeds the engine one TLS record at a time (its header, then its length), never"] [38 1 "// more, so after an unwrap the plain bytes behind close_notify stay in the socket as with OpenSSL. A callback"] [39 1 "// the engine needs (the SNI callback) runs on the Python thread with the GIL. Writes and close_notify, which"] [40 1 "// never wait for input, are made on the Python thread directly once the handshake is done (tls.Conn's write"] [41 1 "// side is independent of its read side)."] [64 1 "// sslEngine is the goroutine side: the tls.Conn and its transport's buffers."] [76 2 "// dead is closed when the SSL object dies (stop): the goroutine, waiting for its next operation or for input,"] [77 2 "// returns (py-final-1126)"] [80 2 "// alert is the description OpenSSL would send, 0 when none: the SNI callback's (its *al; Go's server sends"] [81 2 "// internal_error when GetConfigForClient fails), a failed verification's (ssl_x509err2alert; Go sends"] [82 2 "// bad_certificate). The transport puts it in Go's alert record while that is in the clear: always for the"] [83 2 "// SNI callback (before the server's hello), under TLS 1.2 for a verification."] [119 98 "// a fatal alert in the clear"] [134 1 "// call runs f on the Python thread (from the engine)."] [172 1 "// stop ends the engine's goroutine at its SSL object's death (sslSocketFinalize): a goroutine that waits is a root of"] [173 1 "// Go's collector, and what its stack and its connection's config reach stayed alive with it (py-final-1126)."] [181 1 "// sslSockRef is the engine's reference to its SSL object (the callbacks Go's TLS keeps in the connection's config): the"] [182 1 "// object's address, hidden from Go's collector, so that a goroutine waiting for input no longer holds the object, its"] [183 1 "// context and what they reach (py-final-1126: test_asyncio's TLS tests, an SSL context still alive after a handshake"] [184 1 "// cut short and gc.collect()). The engine calls back only within an operation the object's own method runs (the object"] [185 1 "// held by that call); its death clears the address and stops the engine (sslSocketFinalize)."] [196 1 "// sslSocketFinalize is the SSL object's death (TrackFinalizer): its engine stopped."] [207 1 "// pySSLSocket is an SSL object (PySSLSocket)."] [211 24 "// nil: over MemoryBIOs"] [215 26 "// a weak reference, as _ssl's (queue 241: a dead owner fails the SNI callback)"] [231 24 "// the incoming record being fed, for the message callback"] [232 24 "// the bytes at the head of the engine's output already traced (a socket's unsent rest)"] [233 24 "// the version the message callback reports: the server hello's, once seen"] [237 22 "// 3.15.2's got_eof_error (gh-148292): an SSLEOFError raised, read, write and do_handshake raise it again"] [239 2 "// ref is the engine's weak reference to it (py-final-1126)"] [243 1 "// eofAgain is 3.15.2's set_eof_error: after an SSLEOFError, read, write and do_handshake raise SSLEOFError again with"] [244 1 "// no library and no reason (queue 263; 3.14.10 has no got_eof_error)."] [256 1 "// sslVerifyError is a certificate verification failure: OpenSSL's code and message."] [260 12 "// the alert OpenSSL sends for the code (ssl_x509err2alert), 0 for Go's bad_certificate"] [265 1 "// Unwrap is the alert the vendored crypto/tls sends for the failed verification (queue 552: an AlertError returned by"] [266 1 "// VerifyConnection; Go's own sends bad_certificate, which the transport could rewrite only while in the clear)."] [274 1 "// ---- the session cache of one connection: the session given, the session received ----"] [291 2 "// the session's id: its state's digest, so a resumed session renewed by the server keeps it (OpenSSL keeps"] [292 2 "// the session id across a resumption)"] [309 1 "// ---- the configuration ----"] [314 2 "// queue 552: a PSK suite only with this side's PSK callback (OpenSSL disables kPSK without one)"] [349 3 "// queue 552: SSL_VERIFY_POST_HANDSHAKE, set by newPySSLSocket only with SSL_VERIFY_PEER (bpo-37428): a TLS 1.3"] [350 3 "// client that offered post_handshake_auth is asked for its certificate by verify_client_post_handshake alone"] [376 33 "// SSL_set_post_handshake_auth (queue 552)"] [390 1 "// pskClient is psk_client_callback: the context's callback called on the Python thread with the server's identity"] [391 1 "// hint (None when absent or empty), its (identity, psk) taken as \"z#y#\"; an error unraisable, no PSK offered."] [407 12 "// an invalid UTF-8 hint drops the connection, no exception"] [435 40 "// PSK_MAX_IDENTITY_LEN + 1, PSK_MAX_PSK_LEN"] [446 1 "// pskServer is psk_server_callback: the context's callback called with the client's identity (None when empty), its"] [447 1 "// bytes the key; an error unraisable, the identity refused."] [477 1 "// autoChain is OpenSSL's automatic chain (ssl_add_cert_chain without SSL_MODE_NO_AUTO_CHAIN): a certificate"] [478 1 "// loaded without its chain is sent with the chain the cont